# Commits, README, version

## Commits

Write every commit message in **English**. One declarative line. Never Korean.

```
v0.97: Fade the settings language list with a top and bottom blur.
```

Prefix with `v{VER}` when `app.js` `const VER` moved. Ask before raising VER, committing, pushing, deleting a branch, or `wrangler deploy`.

## README

One file: `README.md`. English, Chinese, Japanese, and Hindi live as consecutive sections in that file. Do not add `README.zh.md` / `README.ja.md` / `README.hi.md`. When docs change, update all four sections.

## Version

`app.js` `VER` goes up by 1 on each change (`0.96 → 0.97`). The **first decimal digit** is the release patch: `VER=0.70` → `v0.3.7`. Never lower a `?v=` query. GitHub Pages source is `static-0.3.X`, not `main`.
